WEBVTT

00:00:05.504 --> 00:00:07.201
[ soprano singing]

00:00:07.244 --> 00:00:12.467
SEAMUS:
Fortuna Major.

00:00:12.511 --> 00:00:13.860
SOPRANO:
♪ Ah, ah, ah, ah...

00:00:13.903 --> 00:00:16.732
Here, listen-- she
just won't let me in.

00:00:16.776 --> 00:00:18.038
Fortuna Major.

00:00:18.081 --> 00:00:19.996
No, no, no, wait. Wait.

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:21.345
Watch this.

00:00:21.389 --> 00:00:22.999
[ clears throat softly]

00:00:23.043 --> 00:00:25.175
♪ Ah, ah, ah...
[ screaming high note]

00:00:25.219 --> 00:00:27.351
[ groaning]

00:00:27.395 --> 00:00:30.616
[ screamed note wavering]

00:00:30.659 --> 00:00:32.356
[ gasps]:
Amazing!

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:34.576
[ chuckles]:
Just with my voice.

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:36.230
Fortuna Major.

00:00:36.273 --> 00:00:37.492
[ stops chuckling]

00:00:37.536 --> 00:00:39.886
Yes, all right. Go in.

00:00:39.929 --> 00:00:41.148
Thank you.

00:00:41.191 --> 00:00:42.454
NEVILLE:
Plebs.

00:00:42.497 --> 00:00:43.629
I can't believe
she's still doing that

00:00:43.672 --> 00:00:44.804
after three years.I know.

00:00:44.847 --> 00:00:45.979
BOTH:
She can't even sing.

00:00:46.022 --> 00:00:47.981
Exactly.Exactly. Unbelievable.

00:00:48.024 --> 00:00:49.156
HARRY:
Hey, man.

00:00:49.199 --> 00:00:50.810
SEAMUS:
Hey, man.

00:00:50.853 --> 00:00:51.898
DEAN THOMAS:
Oh, God!

00:00:51.941 --> 00:00:53.029
HERMIONE:
That's awful.

00:00:53.073 --> 00:00:54.814
RON:
Oh, green.
That's a monkey.

00:00:54.857 --> 00:00:57.207
[ Seamus imitates
monkey chattering]

00:00:57.251 --> 00:00:59.427
[ laughs]:
What is that?

00:00:59.471 --> 00:01:00.863
You call that a monkey?

00:01:00.907 --> 00:01:03.518
Do not give him
one again.

00:01:03.562 --> 00:01:05.520
Hey, Neville,
try an elephant.

00:01:05.564 --> 00:01:07.130
[ thunder crashing]

00:01:07.174 --> 00:01:10.960
[ authentic trumpeting
of an elephant]

00:01:12.527 --> 00:01:13.746
Ron, catch!

00:01:13.789 --> 00:01:15.835
Oh, yeah.

00:01:15.878 --> 00:01:19.360
[ authentic growling of a lion][ boys ooh-ing and ah-ing]

00:01:19.403 --> 00:01:21.014
HARRY:
I think we have a winner.

00:01:21.057 --> 00:01:24.452
[ boys laughing]Oh, don't try one of them!

00:01:24.496 --> 00:01:25.540
Oh, no!

00:01:25.584 --> 00:01:27.020
[ laughter]Look at this.

00:01:27.063 --> 00:01:28.761
Look at his face!

00:01:28.804 --> 00:01:31.546
♪

00:01:35.376 --> 00:01:38.771
[ thunder cracks]

00:01:47.780 --> 00:01:50.043
[ bell tolls]

00:01:50.086 --> 00:01:53.437
[ bird chirping]

00:01:54.743 --> 00:01:57.703
[ chirping continues]

00:02:07.364 --> 00:02:10.411
[ branches creaking,
leaves rustling]

00:02:10.454 --> 00:02:13.719
TRELAWNEY:
Welcome, my children.

00:02:13.762 --> 00:02:19.420
In this room, you shall explore
the noble art of Divination.

00:02:19.463 --> 00:02:23.816
In this room, you shall discover
if you possess

00:02:23.859 --> 00:02:25.513
the Sight.

00:02:25.557 --> 00:02:26.514
[ clattering][ children giggling]

00:02:26.558 --> 00:02:29.865
Hello. I am Professor Trelawney.

00:02:29.909 --> 00:02:34.261
Together, we shall cast
ourselves into the future!

00:02:34.304 --> 00:02:35.610
[ chuckles]

00:02:35.654 --> 00:02:37.177
This term, we shall be
focusing on Tasseomancy,

00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:39.179
which is the art
of reading tea leaves.

00:02:39.222 --> 00:02:40.354
So please, take the cup

00:02:40.397 --> 00:02:42.095
of the person sitting
opposite you.

00:02:42.138 --> 00:02:43.313
[ slurping]

00:02:43.357 --> 00:02:44.532
What do you see?

00:02:44.576 --> 00:02:46.099
The truth lies buried

00:02:46.142 --> 00:02:48.362
like a sentence
deep within a book,

00:02:48.405 --> 00:02:50.886
waiting to be read.

00:02:50.930 --> 00:02:52.409
But first, you must broaden

00:02:52.453 --> 00:02:53.628
your minds.

00:02:53.672 --> 00:02:54.629
First,

00:02:54.673 --> 00:02:56.631
you must look... beyond!

00:02:56.675 --> 00:02:57.893
What a load of rubbish.

00:02:57.937 --> 00:02:59.373
Where did you
come from?!

00:02:59.416 --> 00:03:01.767
Me? I've been here
all this time.

00:03:01.810 --> 00:03:05.205
You, boy-- is your
grandmother quite well?

00:03:05.248 --> 00:03:06.554
Uh, I-I think so.

00:03:06.598 --> 00:03:08.643
I-I wouldn't be
so sure of that.

00:03:08.687 --> 00:03:10.427
Give me the cup.

00:03:11.167 --> 00:03:13.779
Oh... hmm....

00:03:13.822 --> 00:03:14.736
Pity.

00:03:14.780 --> 00:03:17.783
Broaden your minds!

00:03:17.826 --> 00:03:19.480
[ humming]:
Mmm...

00:03:19.523 --> 00:03:20.612
[ gasps]:
Oh!

00:03:20.655 --> 00:03:23.005
Your aura is
pulsing, dear.

00:03:23.049 --> 00:03:24.920
Are you in
the beyond?

00:03:24.964 --> 00:03:26.139
I think you are.

00:03:26.182 --> 00:03:27.531
Sure.

00:03:27.575 --> 00:03:29.272
Look at the cup.
Tell me what you see.

00:03:29.316 --> 00:03:30.317
Oh, yeah, um...

00:03:30.360 --> 00:03:31.623
Well,Mmm...

00:03:31.666 --> 00:03:34.669
Harry's got sort of
a wonky cross.

00:03:34.713 --> 00:03:36.323
That's trials and suffering.

00:03:36.366 --> 00:03:38.978
And, uh, that there
could be the sun,

00:03:39.021 --> 00:03:40.501
and that's happiness.

00:03:40.544 --> 00:03:42.895
So, uh... you're
gonna suffer...

00:03:42.938 --> 00:03:44.287
TRELAWNEY:
Hm?

00:03:44.331 --> 00:03:46.550
...but you're gonna
be happy about it.

00:03:46.594 --> 00:03:47.900
Give me the cup.

00:03:47.943 --> 00:03:49.075
[ gasps, yells]

00:03:49.118 --> 00:03:53.035
[ panting]:
Oh, my dear boy.

00:03:54.210 --> 00:03:57.518
My dear...

00:03:57.561 --> 00:03:58.867
you have...

00:03:58.911 --> 00:04:00.521
the Grim.[ children gasping]

00:04:00.564 --> 00:04:02.697
SEAMUS:
The Grin? What's the Grin?

00:04:02.741 --> 00:04:04.568
BEM:
Not the Grin, you idiot,

00:04:04.612 --> 00:04:05.918
the Grim.

00:04:05.961 --> 00:04:08.311
"Taking form of a
giant spectral dog,

00:04:08.355 --> 00:04:11.663
"it's among the darkest omens
in our world.

00:04:11.706 --> 00:04:13.229
"It's an omen...

00:04:13.273 --> 00:04:15.057
of death."

00:04:18.757 --> 00:04:19.714
[ bell tolls]

00:04:19.758 --> 00:04:21.020
RON:
You don't think

00:04:21.063 --> 00:04:22.325
that Grim thing's
got anything to do

00:04:22.369 --> 00:04:23.500
with Sirius Black,
do you?

00:04:23.544 --> 00:04:25.198
HERMIONE:
Oh, honestly, Ron!

00:04:25.241 --> 00:04:27.026
If you ask me, Divination's
a very woolly discipline.

00:04:27.069 --> 00:04:30.856
Now, Ancient Runes,
that's a fascinating subject.

00:04:30.899 --> 00:04:32.509
Ancient Runes?

00:04:32.553 --> 00:04:34.860
Exactly how many classes
are you taking this term?

00:04:34.903 --> 00:04:36.209
A fair few.

00:04:36.252 --> 00:04:37.036
Hang on.

00:04:37.079 --> 00:04:38.341
That's not possible.

00:04:38.385 --> 00:04:40.082
Ancient Runes
is in the same time

00:04:40.126 --> 00:04:41.301
as Divination.

00:04:41.344 --> 00:04:43.564
You have to be
in two classes at once.

00:04:43.607 --> 00:04:45.044
Don't be silly, Ronald.

00:04:45.087 --> 00:04:46.915
How could anyone be
in two classes at once?

00:04:46.959 --> 00:04:48.351
Broaden your minds!

00:04:48.395 --> 00:04:50.353
[ chuckling]:
Use your inner eye

00:04:50.397 --> 00:04:51.528
to see the future!

00:04:51.572 --> 00:04:53.226
[ chuckles]

00:04:53.269 --> 00:04:54.531
That's it.
Come on, now.

00:04:54.575 --> 00:04:55.750
Come closer.[ chattering]

00:04:55.794 --> 00:04:57.578
Less talking,
if you don't mind.

00:04:57.621 --> 00:04:58.797
Shh! Shh! Shh!

00:04:58.840 --> 00:05:00.015
I got a real treat
for you today.

00:05:00.059 --> 00:05:02.452
A great lesson.
So follow me.

00:05:08.545 --> 00:05:12.898
[ students chattering]

00:05:12.941 --> 00:05:15.030
Right, you lot.
Less chattering.

00:05:15.074 --> 00:05:16.118
Form a group over there.

00:05:16.162 --> 00:05:17.816
And open your books to page 49.

00:05:17.859 --> 00:05:20.166
Exactly how do we do that?

00:05:20.209 --> 00:05:23.735
Well, just stroke the spine,
of course.

00:05:23.778 --> 00:05:25.649
Goodness me.

00:05:27.564 --> 00:05:30.350
[ purring]

00:05:31.655 --> 00:05:32.787
[ book growling]

00:05:32.831 --> 00:05:33.875
[ yells]

00:05:33.919 --> 00:05:34.789
DRACO:Don't be

00:05:34.833 --> 00:05:35.790
such a wimp,
Longbottom.

00:05:35.834 --> 00:05:37.357
I'm okay.
Okay.

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:38.314
[ yells]

00:05:38.358 --> 00:05:40.839
[ low growling]

00:05:40.882 --> 00:05:42.492
I think they're funny.

00:05:42.536 --> 00:05:43.885
DRACO:
Oh, yeah.

00:05:43.929 --> 00:05:44.930
Terribly funny!

00:05:44.973 --> 00:05:46.105
Really witty!

00:05:46.148 --> 00:05:47.628
God, this place has gone
to the dogs!

00:05:47.671 --> 00:05:48.934
Wait until my father hears
that Dumbledore's

00:05:48.977 --> 00:05:50.283
got this oaf teaching classes!

00:05:50.326 --> 00:05:51.458
[ chuckling]

00:05:51.501 --> 00:05:53.721
Shut up, Malfoy.

00:05:53.765 --> 00:05:58.204
ALL:
Ooh!

00:06:07.474 --> 00:06:08.649
D-Dementor!

00:06:08.692 --> 00:06:10.216
Dementor![ students gasping]

00:06:10.259 --> 00:06:13.959
[ laughing]

00:06:14.002 --> 00:06:15.830
Ooh...

00:06:15.874 --> 00:06:16.788
[ laughing]

00:06:16.831 --> 00:06:18.006
Just turn away, Harry.

00:06:18.050 --> 00:06:19.660
You're supposed to

00:06:19.703 --> 00:06:21.140
stroke it.

00:06:21.183 --> 00:06:22.837
Yeah.

00:06:22.881 --> 00:06:25.840
[ clears throat]

00:06:25.884 --> 00:06:28.669
Da-da-da-da!

00:06:29.148 --> 00:06:32.934
[ bleating]

00:06:32.978 --> 00:06:35.981
Isn't he beautiful?

00:06:36.024 --> 00:06:38.679
Say hello to Buckbeak.

00:06:38.722 --> 00:06:41.682
Hagrid, exactly
what is that?

00:06:41.725 --> 00:06:43.205
That, Ron, is a hippogriff.

00:06:43.249 --> 00:06:45.381
First thing you want
to know about hippogriffs

00:06:45.425 --> 00:06:47.819
is that they're
very proud creatures.

00:06:47.862 --> 00:06:49.124
Very easily offended.

00:06:49.168 --> 00:06:52.040
You do not want to insult
a hippogriff.

00:06:52.084 --> 00:06:54.434
It may just be
the last thing you ever do.

00:06:54.477 --> 00:06:56.871
Now... who'd like
to come and say hello?

00:06:56.915 --> 00:06:59.526
[ whispering indistinctly]

00:06:59.569 --> 00:07:02.572
Well done, Harry.
Well done.

00:07:05.837 --> 00:07:08.100
Come on now.

00:07:08.143 --> 00:07:09.362
Now...

00:07:09.405 --> 00:07:11.451
you have to let him make
the first move.

00:07:11.494 --> 00:07:12.539
It's only polite.

00:07:12.582 --> 00:07:13.627
So... you step up.

00:07:13.670 --> 00:07:14.846
Give him a nice bow.

00:07:14.889 --> 00:07:16.282
Then you wait and
see if he bows back.

00:07:16.325 --> 00:07:18.980
And if he does, you
can go and touch him.

00:07:19.024 --> 00:07:20.895
And if not...

00:07:20.939 --> 00:07:23.724
well, we'll get to that later.

00:07:23.767 --> 00:07:28.120
Now, just make
your bow.

00:07:29.121 --> 00:07:31.427
Nice and low.

00:07:32.733 --> 00:07:33.952
[ bleating]

00:07:33.995 --> 00:07:36.041
[ squawks]

00:07:36.084 --> 00:07:38.478
Back off, Harry!
Back off!

00:07:38.521 --> 00:07:39.827
[ snaps]

00:07:39.871 --> 00:07:41.829
Keep still.

00:07:43.004 --> 00:07:45.180
Keep still.

00:07:45.224 --> 00:07:48.618
[ bleating]

00:07:51.708 --> 00:07:52.927
[ chuckles]

00:07:52.971 --> 00:07:54.407
Well done, Harry.

00:07:54.450 --> 00:07:55.930
Well done.

00:07:55.974 --> 00:07:57.801
[ chuckling]:
Eh, you big brute, you.

00:07:57.845 --> 00:07:58.846
[ exhales]

00:07:58.890 --> 00:08:00.195
[ Buckbeak belches]

00:08:00.239 --> 00:08:02.763
Right. Now I think
you can go and pat him now.

00:08:02.806 --> 00:08:05.548
Go on.
Don't be shy.

00:08:08.290 --> 00:08:09.291
Ow!

00:08:09.335 --> 00:08:11.076
[ indistinct voices]

00:08:11.119 --> 00:08:13.774
HAGRID:
Nice and
slow there.

00:08:13.817 --> 00:08:15.036
Nice and slow.

00:08:15.080 --> 00:08:16.385
[ whispers]:
Nice and slow.

00:08:18.344 --> 00:08:20.520
Not so fast, Harry.[ squawks]

00:08:20.563 --> 00:08:22.261
[ gasps]

00:08:23.740 --> 00:08:26.047
HAGRID [ whispering]:
Slow down, Harry.

00:08:26.091 --> 00:08:28.789
That's it.
Nice and slow.

00:08:28.832 --> 00:08:29.964
[ Harry gasps]

00:08:30.008 --> 00:08:32.445
HAGRID:
Now let him come to you.

00:08:32.488 --> 00:08:33.794
That's it.

00:08:33.837 --> 00:08:34.795
Slowly now.

00:08:34.838 --> 00:08:35.796
Slowly, slowly.

00:08:35.839 --> 00:08:37.058
[ low grunting]

00:08:37.102 --> 00:08:39.147
That's it.

00:08:39.191 --> 00:08:40.148
Yes!

00:08:40.192 --> 00:08:41.715
[ claps]

00:08:41.758 --> 00:08:42.977
Well done!

00:08:43.021 --> 00:08:43.978
Oh, well done, Harry!
Well done.

00:08:44.022 --> 00:08:46.285
It's gonna get to fly?

00:08:46.328 --> 00:08:48.678
I think he may let
you ride him now.

00:08:48.722 --> 00:08:49.505
What?!

00:08:49.549 --> 00:08:50.506
Come on.

00:08:50.550 --> 00:08:51.507
Hey, hey, hey,
hey, hey, hey!

00:08:51.551 --> 00:08:52.552
Put you over here.Ha-Hagrid!

00:08:52.595 --> 00:08:53.857
Just behind the wing joint.

00:08:53.901 --> 00:08:55.120
[ squawks]

00:08:55.163 --> 00:08:56.860
Don't pull out
any of his feathers,

00:08:56.904 --> 00:08:58.862
'cause he won't thank you
for that.

00:08:58.906 --> 00:09:00.342
Whoa!
Hey!

00:09:00.386 --> 00:09:01.865
[ chuckles]

00:09:02.692 --> 00:09:04.433
[ panting]

00:09:05.869 --> 00:09:07.567
Whoa!

00:09:07.610 --> 00:09:10.787
[ students shouting]

00:09:13.094 --> 00:09:15.705
[ squawking]

